icacy  of existing vaccines and and how long  could it take um to adjust them so that  they can then tackle this new variant  i'm pretty confident that like with  previous variants and even if this new  variant omicron is is even worse than  the previous ones  the vaccines will still retain a very  good degree of protection against severe  disease and death so i fully concur with  professor drosten that being vaccinated  is the way to be and getting a booster  dose when you are eligible for a booster  dose is also the best thing to do  however it may of course reduce the  protective effect of the vaccines but it  is possible to twist to tweak these  vaccines in order to accommodate a new  variant and i hear that this is  happening already that's one of the  advantages of modern science where we  can have the sequences uh within a day  or two they are becoming available  worldwide and they are  then used by the manufacturers to to  look at new vaccines however it will be  several months if until the new vaccine  becomes available so you know don't  expect any quick solution and it's  certainly not a reason not to have your  uh basic immunization or your booster  dose right now  now since omicron was first reported  many countries have restricted travel  from southern africa south africa's  president says his country is being  unfairly punished would you say that  travel bans are effective and  appropriate now  well i'm worried about uh hearing so  many cases being detected  in fact this is why we sounded the alarm  bell early we wanted to give other  countries the chance to be on the  lookout for this new variant and that is  happening  um and yes i agree that it feels like  south africa is being punished for doing  what all countries should ideally be  doing i.e look at the evolution of the  virus in their population and give  alerts to other countries as early as  possible also we are doing that and we  didn't want to create panic we wanted to  give an advance warn